        "source": "autotrader",
        "whyGood": "Only 34,000 miles on a 2001 CLK 430 Cabriolet is exceptional \u2014 the V8 engine has barely been broken in. The CLK soft-top is a proper 4-seat Mercedes convertible with a simple, reliable hydraulic top system. The W208 CLK is widely considered the last 'pure' Mercedes \u2014 pre-complexity, pre-electronic overengineering. At $11,990 with 34K miles, this is the best deal in the pool.",
        "whatToVerify": "Full top cycle test (raise/lower 3x, listen for hydraulic pump strain). Check headliner fabric for water staining and rear seat carpet dampness. Inspect rear window seam carefully \u2014 delamination is common. Look for rust on sill plates and under rear bumper. Rocker panels on W208 can rust from the inside out. Verify timing chain guide condition on the 4.3L V8 (one-time chain tensioner check at PPI). Check all electric window regulators and sunroof function.",
        "bottomLine": "Best-value pick of the refresh \u2014 34K miles on a V8 Mercedes cabriolet at under $12K is a find."
      },
