        "source": "cars.com",
        "whyGood": "46,000 miles on a 1995 Jaguar XJS 4.0 convertible is remarkable low-mileage territory for a '90s British classic. The XJS 2+2 is genuinely a 4-seat car, and the straight-six (4.0L AJ6/AJ16) is Jaguar's most reliable engine from this era. This car has clean title and no accidents per the search filters. At under $10K with only 46K miles, this is the most miles-per-dollar value in the pool.",
        "whatToVerify": "Comprehensive PPI at a Jaguar specialist. Full convertible top operation and hydraulic ram inspection. Check for weeping power steering and coolant hoses (they're 30 years old). Inspect undercarriage for rust \u2014 Pennsylvania salt exposure matters. Verify all electric window lifts, the central locking, and AC compressor function. Ask for service history \u2014 XJS needs regular coolant flushes and oil changes to stay healthy. Budget $300-500 for immediate coolant hoses as preventative.",
        "bottomLine": "A time-capsule British convertible at 46K miles \u2014 incredible value if the PPI comes back clean."
